@CLS@SETTING UP YOUR BOARD
--------------------------------------
CONFIG on its own lists the pages.
CONFIG and a page name opens one, so
CONFIG board is the first. F1 saves a
page; most changes apply at once.

BOARD
The board's name, its hostname on the
network, the timezone and NTP server,
idle minutes, the LED pin, and where
callers land after login.

LIMITS
Minutes per call and per day, the WHO
refresh, and the account cap.

ACCOUNTS
Whether callers may sign up, whether
guests may call, and for how long.

Page 1 of 3
BACKUP
The port, how long the window stays
open, and the button pin.

STAFF
The passwords you just set.

WIFI
The network. A change is used from
the next restart, never live.

THE PLUGINS
One page each: chat, forums, files,
info, announce and sd. Each starts
with whether it is on and who may
use it.

Page 2 of 3
THE CARD
File areas and the forums live on an
SD card, so neither exists without
one. A board meant to stay up should
have a card. CONFIG sd has the pins.

OPENING UP
Callers see a closed sign until
CONFIG board's last row says no.
CONFIG announce lists the board in
the public directory, off until you
switch it on. Port forwarding last.

STAFF COMMANDS
SYS         the board's health
DASH        the live dashboard
USERS       the accounts
HELP STAFF  the staff commands
HELP SYSOP  yours alone
The setup guide at unleashedbbs.com
has the rest. Welcome aboard.
